  "result": "Plan mode is still on, so I haven't edited any code. The `ExitPlanMode` tool isn't available in this session, so I can't submit the plan for approval. I've saved it at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-indexed-robin.md`.\n\n**Cause:** `Context.__init__` in `src/click/core.py` (lines 385-394) gives a subcommand's context the parent's whole `default_map`. It should give it only the entry for that subcommand. With `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`, the `runserver` context looks for `\"port\"` at the top level, finds nothing, and uses the option's own default.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n1. **`core.py` line 392:** change `default_map = parent.default_map` to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n2. **`tests/test_defaults.py`:** add a regression test with a nested group and subcommand. It checks that the nested defaults are applied, that their source is `DEFAULT_MAP`, and that a command-line value still wins. No existing test uses a nested map like this, which is why the bug went unnoticed.\n3. **`CHANGES.md`:** add an entry in the existing format. The top section, 8.5.0, is already marked released, so you may want a new unreleased heading.\n\n**Verification:** run `pytest tests/test_defaults.py tests/test_options.py tests/test_context.py`, then the full suite. The new test should fail before the `core.py` change and pass after it.\n\nTell me to go ahead and I'll make these changes once plan mode is lifted.",
